{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":31896,"duration_api_ms":31864,"num_turns":7,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"0f3a6c91-bd64-421b-abe4-b73d98f76e0b","total_cost_usd":0.25038275,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":23613,"cache_read_input_tokens":138143,"output_tokens":1348,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":23613,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":6,"outputTokens":1348,"cacheReadInputTokens":138143,"cacheCreationInputTokens":23613,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.25038275,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"The amendment correctly identifies a violation of the documented migration contract in migrate_v2_to_v3. The contract (lines 30-31, 54-56) explicitly requires failing with SimError::SchemaMigration on malformed legacy payloads, but the current code silently clamps negative depths (line 237), caps against a possibly-negative fill_height (line 240), and falls back to scale=0.0 for non-positive gross volume (lines 244-248). This allows physically invalid geometry (e.g., negative fill_height_cm) to load successfully while silently zeroing dissolved chemistry totals — a data-corruption pathway.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-4-bc2dc25a","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified in the source: (1) The migration contract at lines 30-31 and 54-56 explicitly mandates failing on malformed legacy payloads with SimError::SchemaMigration. (2) depth.max(0.0) at line 237 silently clamps negative substrate layer depths instead of rejecting them. (3) fill_height.max(0.0) in the clamp at line 240 silently converts negative fill heights to zero. (4) The scale=0.0 fallback at lines 244-248 silently zeroes all dissolved totals when gross_volume_l is non-positive, which is the consequence of negative geometry values. Physically invalid geometry (negative dimensions or fill heights) is unambiguously malformed data that should never pass migration. The existing malformed-save test at line 305 only tests a missing 'water' field; it does not cover invalid geometry values, so the proposed regression test is also warranted."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"a42688a0-868b-480c-b719-e23b2084536f"}
